  "reason": "The current best is config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) at 0.713 acc. The image modality contributed ~0.06 over RNA-only (0.653→0.713), but image-alone with resnet50 was very weak (0.208), suggesting resnet50 features may be suboptimal for this task. Config_039 is a clean single-variable test: it swaps the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other settings (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion) identical to the best config. This isolates the effect of image representation quality on multimodal fusion. If ViT-L provides richer visual features, it could push accuracy above 0.713. This is the highest-impact untested variable given that fusion type (weighted vs concat) and aggregation (transformer vs avgpool) showed minimal differences in RNA-only experiments, whereas the image encoder has not been varied in the multimodal setting."
